# Your settings. `npm run setup` copies this to .env.local and fills in the API key.
# .env.local stays on your computer: it's never committed.

# Required: your Anthropic API key (console.anthropic.com → Settings → API Keys)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Spending protection (optional; these are the defaults)
# DAILY_LIMIT_USD=10
# MONTHLY_LIMIT_USD=40
# REVIEW_COST_CAP_USD=3
# MAX_REVIEWS_PER_DAY=8
# MAX_FOLLOWUPS_PER_REVIEW=20
# MAX_ANSWER_CHECKS_PER_HOUR=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: accounts with Supabase (see README "Optional: accounts with Supabase").
# Leave these out to run in local mode: no sign-in, everything stays on this computer.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# Your own Postgres or Supabase database. Leave out to use the built-in one (data/pg).
# DATABASE_URL=
# Your login email(s), comma-separated, to see the app's API spend on Your reviews
# OWNER_EMAILS=
# Ceilings for one network across all its accounts (defaults shown)
# MAX_REVIEWS_PER_NETWORK_PER_DAY=40
# MAX_ANSWER_CHECKS_PER_NETWORK_PER_HOUR=300

# Advanced (optional)
# DATA_DIR=          where media and the built-in database live (default ./data)
# Where browsers get the speech-to-text model and its runtime. Built into the pages, so set them
# before `npm run build`. Defaults: Hugging Face and jsDelivr (version pinned in src/media/browser/cdn.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MODEL_HOST=https://huggingface.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ORT_WASM_BASE=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/onnxruntime-web@<version>/dist/
# PORT=              default 3000
# HOST=              default 127.0.0.1 (this computer only; keep it that way)
# (Local mode needs neither TRUSTED_PROXIES nor CLIENT_IP_HEADER: it's one person on this computer.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted mode: running Panel as a public website (Render first, Fly.io second; docs/hosting.md).
# Leave all of this out to run Panel on your own computer (local mode).
# On a host, set these in its environment (Render: the service's Environment tab, asked for when
# you apply render.yaml; Fly: `fly secrets set NAME=value`), not in a file.
#
# PANEL_MODE=hosted     "local" (the default) or "hosted". Anything else stops Panel at startup.
#
# Hosted mode won't start without every one of these, and says which are missing:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY,
#   DATABASE_URL (see the accounts section above), KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET, MEDIA_SECRET, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET (below), and:
# HOSTED_PUBLIC_URL=https://panel.example.com
#                       The site's public https address, nothing after it. Sign-in sends people
#                       back here, so in Supabase set Authentication → URL Configuration → Site URL
#                       to it and add <it>/** under Redirect URLs. Open the site at this address only.
#                       The NEXT_PUBLIC_ settings are built into the pages, so they must also be set
#                       when `npm run build` runs (Render passes them to the Docker build itself;
#                       on Fly, as build arguments).
# KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET=
#                       Encrypts the Anthropic API keys people save to pay with their own key
#                       (AES-256-GCM). 32 random bytes as base64 or hex. Make one with:
#                         openssl rand -base64 32
#                       Keep it secret and keep it safe: if it's lost or changed, saved keys
#                       can't be read and people have to save theirs again.
# MEDIA_SECRET=
#                       Signs the links to review media and keys the per-network limits. At least 32
#                       random bytes as base64 or hex. Make one with:
#                         openssl rand -base64 32
#                       It must be the same on every machine and across restarts, or
#                       links break and per-network limits reset. Local mode doesn't use it (it keeps
#                       its own secret in the data folder).
# MAX_KEY_CHECKS_PER_HOUR=10  tries at saving a key, per account (each one asks Anthropic)
#
# Prepaid credits, bought with Stripe Checkout (docs/billing.md). Hosted mode won't start without both:
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=    Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API keys → Secret key (sk_live_… or sk_test_…;
#                       a restricted key, rk_…, needs write access to Checkout Sessions).
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#                       Stripe Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → add an endpoint at
#                       <HOSTED_PUBLIC_URL>/api/stripe/webhook sending checkout.session.completed,
#                       checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded, charge.refunded and
#                       charge.dispute.created, then copy its signing secret (whsec_…).
# FOLLOWUP_COST_CAP_USD=1.5   the most one follow-up answer may cost on credits. Each review sets
#                       aside REVIEW_COST_CAP_USD x 1.2 and each answer this x 1.2 while it runs.
#
# Uploads. The browser prepares each video (a 720p copy, stills, a transcript) and sends those
# files; MAX_UPLOAD_MB is the biggest prepared video, in megabytes (default 50 in hosted mode,
# Supabase Free's per-file cap; 250 on your own computer). In hosted mode the files go straight
# to the private review-media storage bucket at one-time addresses, and the website checks them
# before anything paid runs. Without SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY and the Supabase URL, uploads say so and stop.
# MAX_UPLOAD_MB=50
#
# Where the website listens. `npm start` in hosted mode defaults to every interface, which is what
# the host's proxy needs (the standalone server.js in the Docker image listens on HOSTNAME and PORT,
# set in the Dockerfile; render.yaml sets PORT=8080, and Fly's internal_port in fly.toml must match PORT).
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=3000
#
# Who is visiting. Behind a proxy every request arrives from the proxy, so per-person limits
# need one of these, or hosted mode won't start. A visitor can send any X-Forwarded-For they like,
# so it's only used the way TRUSTED_PROXIES describes. (Local mode ignores both: one person.)
#   CLIENT_IP_HEADER  a header your host overwrites on every request with the visitor's address.
#                     Render: CF-Connecting-IP (Render serves sites through Cloudflare).
#                     Fly: Fly-Client-IP. Cloudflare: CF-Connecting-IP. Only use a header your
#                     host always replaces; any other header could be made up by the visitor.
#   TRUSTED_PROXIES   or, the number of proxies in front of Panel that each append to X-Forwarded-For
#                     (Fly: 1). Panel takes the Nth entry from the right, the address the outermost
#                     of them saw; everything to its left is what the visitor wrote and is ignored.
#                     Only safe if the site can't be reached except through those proxies.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=Fly-Client-IP
